BarkernotBob/logos-notes.body:
**What you asked for**

Plug-and-play publishing: users shouldn't have to ask Isaiah for the Logos App Key/Secret. Options:
- (a) ship the OAuth 1.0a consumer key/secret in the extension (Raycast Store source is public, so the secret becomes public; per-user sign-in still protects notes, but misuse could get the app revoked for everyone);
- (b) small signing server holding the secret (every request incl. note text would pass through it, since OAuth 1.0a signs every call);
- (c) ask Faithlife for permission to ship the key or for a public-client flow (OAuth2 + PKCE).

Recommended: ask Faithlife first, then (a) if allowed, (b) only if refused. Read-only Logos→Obsidian sync already needs no keys. Needs grilling before building.
